 ```

+#### signal
+
+Type: `AbortSignal`
+
+Cancel queued tasks when the signal is aborted.
+
+Queued tasks are rejected with the signal's abort reason, and any task added after the signal is aborted is rejected immediately without running. This happens regardless of the `rejectOnClear` option.
+
+Note: This does not cancel tasks that are already running. Pass the signal on to the task itself if you need that.
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 1, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const results = Promise.allSettled([
+	limit(() => fetchSomething('foo')),
+	limit(() => fetchSomething('bar'))
+]);
+
+// Only `foo` runs; `bar` is still queued and rejects with the abort reason.
+controller.abort();
+
+console.log(await results);
+```
+
 ### limit(fn, ...args)

 Returns the promise returned by calling `fn(...args)`.
